---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Footer from "../components/Footer.astro";

const lastUpdated = "June 24, 2026";
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy Policy — AllByte Studios">
  <main class="legal-page">
    <article class="legal-body">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated: {lastUpdated}</p>

      <p>
        This site (<strong>allbyte.studio</strong>) is operated by AllByte
        Studios, a solo independent game developer (referred to here as
        &ldquo;I,&rdquo; &ldquo;me,&rdquo; or &ldquo;AllByte&rdquo;). This policy
        explains what information I collect when you visit the site, log in, or
        play <em>The Chronicles of Nesis</em>, and how I handle it. I keep data
        collection to the minimum needed to run the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Information I collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Account information (via Patreon).</strong> Logging in is
          handled entirely through Patreon. When you authorize the connection, I
          receive your Patreon user ID, your name, your email address, and your
          current membership tier. I store these to identify your account and to
          unlock the content your tier grants.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Cloud save data.</strong> If you choose to sync your game
          progress, the save data you upload is stored so it can be restored on
          your other devices. Saves are only synced when you opt in.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Technical data.</strong> Like any website, my hosting and
          content-delivery layer (Amazon Web Services / CloudFront) records
          standard request logs &mdash; IP address, browser type, and the pages
          requested &mdash; used for security and to keep the site running.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Browser storage.</strong> I store a login token and a few
          interface preferences (such as music-player state) in your browser's
          local/session storage. These stay on your device.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Release notifications (optional).</strong> If you ask to be
          told when the next Episode is playable, I store the email address you
          give me, which page you asked from, and the dates you signed up and
          confirmed. Nothing is added to the list until you click the
          confirmation link I send, so an address entered by mistake or by
          someone else simply expires. This list is used for one thing only:
          telling you a release is out. It is never sold or shared, and every
          email carries a one-click unsubscribe. You do not need an account, and
          this is kept separate from any Patreon account you may have.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Anonymous gameplay analytics.</strong> When you play in the
          browser, I record anonymous, aggregate progress signals &mdash; a
          random session identifier (kept only for the current tab, not a
          tracking cookie), which scenes you reach, how long you played, and the
          referring site&rsquo;s domain (for example &ldquo;reddit.com&rdquo;).
          This is not linked to your account or identity; I use it only to
          understand where players drop off so I can improve the game.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How I use it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To authenticate you and keep you signed in.</li>
        <li>To grant the site and game features your membership tier includes.</li>
        <li>To sync and restore your game saves when you opt in.</li>
        <li>
          To understand, in aggregate, how far players get in the browser game
          so I can improve it.
        </li>
        <li>To operate, secure, and troubleshoot the site.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I do not sell your personal information, and I do not use it for
        third-party advertising.
      </p>

      <h2>Payments</h2>
      <p>
        All memberships and payments are processed entirely by
        <strong>Patreon</strong>. I never receive, see, or store your card
        number or any other payment details. Patreon's handling of that data is
        governed by <a href="https://privacy.patreon.com/" rel="noopener">Patreon's
        own privacy policy</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Service providers</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>Patreon</strong> &mdash; account login, membership, and payment
          processing.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Amazon Web Services</strong> &mdash; website hosting, storage,
          and the backend that powers login and cloud saves.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        These providers process data only to deliver their part of the service.
      </p>

      <h2>Data retention</h2>
      <p>
        I keep your account information for as long as your account exists. Cloud
        saves are retained until you overwrite or delete them, or until your
        account is removed. Server logs are retained for a limited period for
        security and operational purposes.
      </p>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          You can revoke this site's access to your Patreon account at any time
          from your Patreon account settings.
        </li>
        <li>
          You can request access to, or deletion of, the personal information
          tied to your account by emailing me (see below).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Children</h2>
      <p>
        This site is not directed to children under 13, and I do not knowingly
        collect personal information from them.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Login tokens are signed and transmitted over HTTPS, and passwords are not
        stored on my systems (login is delegated to Patreon). No method of
        transmission or storage is perfectly secure, but I take reasonable steps
        to protect your information.
      </p>

      <h2>Changes</h2>
      <p>
        I may update this policy as the site evolves. The &ldquo;last
        updated&rdquo; date above reflects the current version.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy or your data? Email
        <a href="mailto:allbytestudios@gmail.com">allbytestudios@gmail.com</a>.
      </p>
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer theme="engine" />
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .legal-page {
    background: #1a1e26;
    color: #e0e7ff;
    min-height: 80dvh;
    padding: 3rem 1.25rem;
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
  }

  .legal-body {
    max-width: 46rem;
    width: 100%;
    font-family: "Courier New", Courier, monospace;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  h1 {
    font-family: "AllByteCustom", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 2.25rem;
    color: #a7f3d0;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-family: "AllByteCustom", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    color: #a7f3d0;
    margin: 2.25rem 0 0.5rem;
  }

  .updated {
    color: rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.5);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.5rem;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: rgba(224, 231, 255, 0.82);
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  li {
    margin: 0.4rem 0;
  }

  a {
    color: #a7f3d0;
  }

  strong {
    color: #e0e7ff;
  }
</style>
